// ==========================================
// INDEX COMMENTS & NOTES
// ==========================================
// Note: In actual SQL, indices should be created for:
// - All `tenant_id` and `branch_id` columns to support fast RLS and multi-tenant queries.
// - All foreign key columns.
// - Frequently searched columns like `email`, `phone_number`, `order_number`, `po_number`.
// - Date/Timestamp columns used in reporting (e.g., `orders.created_at`, `bills.created_at`, `inventory_transactions.created_at`).
//
// Partitioning Strategy:
// - `orders`, `order_items`: Partition by `created_at` (monthly)
// - `inventory_transactions`: Partition by `created_at` (monthly)
// - `audit_logs`: Partition by `created_at` (monthly)
//
// Archiving:
// - Move `orders`, `bills`, and related history older than 1 year to archive tables or cold storage to maintain performance.
// - Soft deletes (`deleted_at`) should be purged periodically if compliance permits.
